Q: can you tell me how is this linking happening of Todo.java class TodoController methods and updateTodoPage.jsp 

This is a very good question.
If you understand this, Spring MVC stops feeling like “magic”.
It alone can clear your most of SpringMVC concepts.

1️⃣ THE THREE ACTORS

You have three things:

	Todo.java → plain Java object (data holder)
	TodoController → request handler
	updateTodo.jsp → view (form)

They are not directly linked to each other.
👉 The linking is done by Spring MVC infrastructure, not by your code.


2️⃣ ENTRY POINT: HTTP REQUEST
Example URL:
	/update-todo?id=3	
	Tomcat receives the request → hands it to DispatcherServlet.

3️⃣ DISPATCHERSERVLET (THE BRAIN)

DispatcherServlet does the following:
	Finds the matching controller method for url.
	Calls that method
	Collects:
	Model data
	View name
	Forwards to the JSP
	
This is the Front Controller pattern.


4️⃣ CONTROLLER → MODEL LINK (CRITICAL STEP)

Controller (GET)
		@GetMapping("update-todo")
		public String showUpdateTodoPage(@RequestParam int id, ModelMap model) {
		    Todo todo = todoService.findById(id);
		    model.put("todo", todo);
		    return "updateTodo";
		}

What happens here

	todoService.findById(id) returns a Todo object
	model.put("todo", todo) stores it in the Model
	Key name = "todo"
	ModelMap is a HashMap maintained by SpringMVC
This is the only place where the link is created.


5️⃣ MODEL → JSP LINK (modelAttribute)
	
	In updateTodo.jsp:
	
		<form:form modelAttribute="todo">
	
	This line means:
				“Spring, give me the object named todo from the model.”
	
	Spring does this internally:
				model.get("todo") → Todo object
	
	Now the JSP has access to the Todo instance.

6️⃣ TODO → FORM FIELD LINK (through path attribute)
	
		<form:input path="description"/>
	
	This means:
		Look for getDescription() on the Todo object
	
	Use its value to prefill the input
	
	So:
		todo.getDescription() → input value ( preFilled value comes from here )
	
	This way using todo.get_() all inputs fields are mapped directly to Todo class attributes
	This is object → view binding. ( MOST IMPORTANT ) 

7️⃣ FORM SUBMIT: JSP → CONTROLLER LINK (2nd Most Imp)
	
	User clicks Update → POST request sent.
	
	Payload example:
	
		id=3
		description=Learn Spring MVC
		done=true

8️⃣ SPRING BINDS FORM BACK TO TODO

  Controller POST method:

	@PostMapping("update-todo")
	public String updateTodo(
	        @Valid @ModelAttribute("todo") Todo todo,
	        BindingResult result
	) { 
			What Spring does internally:
			
			Creates a Todo object
			
			Calls:
				setId(3)
				setDescription("Learn Spring MVC")
				setDone(true)
				
			Runs validation
			
			Stores errors in BindingResult }
			
			This is also view → object binding.

9️⃣ WHY JSP STILL KNOWS ABOUT ERRORS

In JSP:

	<form:errors path="description"/>

Spring:
	
	Finds BindingResult for "todo"
	
	Finds errors for description
	
	Renders them
	
	No manual wiring needed.

🔁 COMPLETE LINKING LOOP (MEMORIZE THIS)
	Request
		 1→ DispatcherServlet
		 2→ Controller
		 3→ Model ("todo")
		 4→ JSP (modelAttribute)
		 5→ path → getters
		 6→ Form Submit
		 7→ setters
		 8→ Validation
		 9→ BindingResult
		 10→ JSP errors
